alright give me final v2 schema

I think after our discussion, we can make something much cleaner than a typical RAG schema.

The biggest mistake most RAG projects make is that every knowledge card has a different structure.

I wouldn't do that.

I would make every V2 object follow the same envelope, and only the content field changes depending on the concept type.

That gives you:

one database schema,
one review interface,
one embedding pipeline,
one retrieval pipeline.
Final V2 Architecture
V2/
│
├── definitions/
├── rights/
├── obligations/
├── procedures/
├── authorities/
├── jurisdiction/
├── remedies/
├── penalties/
├── timelines/
├── evidence/
├── exceptions/
├── offences/
├── examples/
├── intents/
├── aliases/
└── relationships/

These folders are only for organization.

Internally every JSON follows exactly the same schema.

Universal V2 Schema
{
    "concept_id": "",

    "concept_type": "",

    "title": "",

    "description": "",

    "content": {},

    "derived_from": [],

    "related_concepts": [],

    "search": {
        "keywords": [],
        "aliases": [],
        "user_queries": []
    },

    "metadata": {
        "jurisdiction": "India",
        "act": "Consumer Protection Act, 2019",
        "language": "en",
        "review_status": "draft",
        "confidence": 0.0,
        "created_by": "DefinitionAgent",
        "reviewed_by": null,
        "version": 1
    }
}

Notice

Only one field changes:

"content":{}

Everything else remains identical.

